&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audio log entry-Dr. Dravis-date(𶐉𶐉𶐉𶐉𶐿𶐉)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Dravis&lt;/strong&gt;-It’s been two months since our divorce, and I’m quite low on myself,&lt;br /&gt;
I need a job I need an opportunity I need a sense of purpose I need the job with Todd, this might be hope for me, a silver bullet&lt;br /&gt;
End audio log&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audio log entry-dr. Dravis – date (𶐉𶐉𶐉𶐉𶐿𶐉)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Dravis&lt;/strong&gt;-Thank goodness, thank goodness Todd accepted me as an assistant in his project.&lt;br /&gt;
Todd told me on their project about a subterranean cave, details would be given when I am hired,&lt;br /&gt;
The man they worked for was a man named Jacqe Pierre in Kazakhstan, I asked if I would join, Todd told me that tomorrow, I would be accepted&lt;br /&gt;
End audio log&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Journal entry-Dr. Todd-date (𶐉𶐉𶐉𶐉𶐿𶐉)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
I required an assistant, I had Edward and Jim working, but I need someone, someone with the same experiences as me. That’s why I persuaded Jacqe to hire him.&lt;br /&gt;
On our exploit, the equipment informed us of the size of the cavity, the statistics suggest that the total length would be around that of the Manhattan island, as it would be as high as at least 200 meters!&lt;br /&gt;
The equipment also indicated water and flora.&lt;br /&gt;
End journal entry&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Journal entry-Dr. Dravis-date(𶐉𶐉𶐉𶐉𶐿𶐉)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Must be fungi, I thought in the morning after thinking about it overnight, which nonetheless made me more excited about the idea that the cave may be pent up with methane as I write!&lt;br /&gt;
It’s only a thought but there’s a high chance that it might be. Minutes later I went to Todd’s and told him about my theory about the cave having fungi, Todd exited with my theory called Jim, and we went to have lunch at Edward’s. there we stayed speculating, theorizing, and talking about the cavity and its contents.&lt;br /&gt;
Three days later we concluded, that at some point in time it was a subterranean river, bringing spores underneath through the river, the spores grow.&lt;br /&gt;
And as the cave grew in size, the fungi grew in numbers until such time it became self-sustaining. The mushrooms might have thrived to such extent that they evolved in the lack of light so when the river was enclosed the contents remained self-sustaining, the dead fungi released methane and fungi drew on the dead fungi and that’s how it stayed for years, until now.&lt;br /&gt;
Our plan was simple we drill a hole in the roof of the cavity, a plant above will suck the theorized methane, convert it through a series of complex machinery that turns the methane into electricity for the years to come, backup generators will be plugged if the output electricity will be too excessive.&lt;br /&gt;
We had planned this for months now.&lt;br /&gt;
It will work.&lt;br /&gt;
It should have. We checked the machine, nothing was wrong, we decided to check the pipes.&lt;br /&gt;
Turns out the methane in the cave was not enough to power the generators, we decided to turn off the plant, jacqe enraged by this demanded that we would check the cave if anything in there might still be of use. Three days later, so here I am writing my journal, a few moments later Todd comes in and tells me that the equipment is ready.&lt;br /&gt;
End journal entry&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5267 debriefing logs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;**Audio log entry-Interviewer-Dr. mercer -Interviewee-dr. Edward -date (𶐉𶐉𶐉𶐉𶐿𶐉Redacted)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;-so you’re a novice of whom?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;-o, o, of Todd sir, of sir Todd’s&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(writing sounds)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;- so, what happened to professor Todd Rey?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;- three hours ago sir be-before y-you, you came for us h-he was, he was-&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;-He was attacked?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;-(nods), y-yes sir&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(moment of silence)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;- I’m truly sorry for your loss&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;-it’s okay, it wasn’t your fault sir&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;- well Edward, you and your professors here have quite a breakthrough here Edward, we may&lt;br /&gt;
be able to help you&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;- it’s all right sir w-we have Jacqe&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;- Pierre? We work with Pierre&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;- oh so he sent you?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;-(shrugs), more or less&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(moment of silence)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;- listen here Edward, we would like to hear about your incident, we would like to hear it from you&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;- well sir had you asked sir Dravis?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;- well no, not quite, he’s still being counseled&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;- oh&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(moment of silence)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;- well Edward would you like to talk about it or would you like to talk at a different time&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;- probably for the best sir&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;- well then would after dinner do?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;-after dinner would do sir&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;End audio log&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The next hour, Mercer requested an interview with Dr. Dravis&lt;br /&gt;
Dr. Dravis denied, stating that he would talk after Edward had&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audio log entry-Interviewer-Dr. Mercer-Interviewee- Dr. Edward Date (𶐉𶐉𶐉𶐉𶐿𶐉)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;- good evening Edward&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;- good evening sir&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;- would you please continue on the topic we’ve picked up last time&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;- of course sir&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;- please proceed then&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;- well it was five days ago when the plant didn’t work as planned, actually it didn’t work at all, we checked the valves but it seemed that the methane was not enough, so three days later we-&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;- would you please elaborate on the plant, and what it should have done?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;- oh, of course.&lt;br /&gt;
(moment of silence)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;- please proceed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;- well I’m trying to remember, the thing it was just, went so fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;- I understand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;- Okay.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(moment of silence)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;- Alright, I got it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;- Proceed&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;- for a start sir we picked up traces of flora in the cave and knowing how caves form, we speculated that by now it would have been pent up with methane, potential energy, just sitting there waiting to be harvested, so that’s what we did, we harvested.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;-I see, please continue&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;- well sir three days later we checked on the cave personally, as Jacqe’s wish, we went down on a buggy in the cave we dug all those months ago, whilst wearing gas masks, heat resistant suits, oxygen tanks, sample vials, flashlights, an 800-foot rope ladder, Todd had a laser cutter in his forearm, and sir Dravis had a satchel, we wen-&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;- what did the satchel contain?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;- oh, h-his journal sir, and a pen&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;- oh, I see please continue&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;-we stopped at a dead end and went to the side of the tunnel, the tunnel had lights all over so we stayed our flashlights at the ready, Todd told us that we were at the top side of the cavity, he engaged his laser cutter, and started cutting a hole on the wall, and have pushed it, falling into an endless abyss,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If it were not for the light.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer&lt;/strong&gt;-light?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt;-(nods), it was such a beautiful sight, sir imagine expecting a half-assed shit hole only to see the oversight of a beautiful grass plain, the water-holes, the green grass, and a couple of forest patches, the light-brown walls covered with thousands of glimmering crystals just imagine heaven when we expected a shit-hole&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(chuckles)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;one can only imagine our emotions akin to those I&#039;m sure of Columbus&#039; sighting on the new world, as Jim managed to say under his breath “ exquisite, h-how?”. Todd said “fascinating, we need to study this”. Dravis with keen eyes, Saw a concrete facility just two klicks away, I grabbed my binoculars and confirmed Dravis’ claim, Jim requested that we camp there, we looked at Jim and Todd said, “good idea lets go now” before we could say anything Todd took some rope, tied it on the wall and went down enthusiastically, he motioned us to go down, Dravis and Jim followed enthusiastically, I hesitantly followed.&lt;/p&gt;
