					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5587</guid>
				<title>SCP-5587</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5587</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;scp-image-block block-right&quot; style=&quot;width:300px;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/scp-5587/Rift&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--resized-images/scp-5587/Rift/medium.jpg&quot; style=&quot;width:300px;&quot; alt=&quot;Rift&quot; class=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;scp-image-caption&quot; style=&quot;width:300px;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5587&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item #:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5587&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object Class:&lt;/strong&gt; Safe&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5587 is to be monitored by six standardized trail cameras positioned within a twenty meter radius of the tree. Edmund’s Path Trailhead is to be closed under the pretense of trail maintenance and unsafe geographical features. Any unauthorized persons monitored near SCP-5587’s site should be detained and given Class-A amnestics before being released from Foundation custody.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5587-1 through -6 are contained together in one furnished humanoid containment cell fitted with a regulated pipe pumping argon into the atmosphere. Requests from each subject are to be approved or denied by Researcher Lawson. Subjects are permitted to visit the staff gym once a week equipped with an argon breathing tank and the accompaniment of a Level 1 researcher or higher to monitor the data relating to their increasing physical abilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5587 is a gateway to an alternate dimension (SCP-5587-A) set into the trunk of an oak tree located on Mount Eisenhower at elevation of 4203 ft in White Mountain National Park, New Hampshire. When an organism comes in contact with SCP-5587, it is pulled through the tree into SCP-5587-A.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5587-A geographically mirrors the appearance of White Mountain National Park. Despite geographical accuracy, flora found in SCP-5587-A do not resemble any known species of fungi or plant. The tallest flora simulate trees and are turquoise colored while possessing smooth surfaces, drooping branches and visible roots stretching across the fungal forest floor. Shorter flora found in SCP-5587-A are a number of highly saturated colors including orange, magenta, blue and yellow. SCP-5587-A’s atmosphere is composed of 79.5% argon, 5% water vapor, 5% other noble gases and a 10.5% concentration of unidentifiable&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-119076-1&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; elements. Elemental compositions of the flora are primarily neon, argon and other unidentifiable elements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5587-B is an ursine resembling entity that resides in SCP-5587-A, showing hostile and predatory behavior toward those who enter the dimension. It stands a height of 3 meters from the withers and is covered in shaggy turquoise fur with prominent yellow canines and large incisors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5587-1, SCP-5587-2, SCP-5587-3, SCP-5587-4, SCP-5587-5 and SCP-5587-6 are Jamie, Nickleson, Bridger, Polonskye, Alejo and White, the former members of Mobile Task Force Zeta-12, “Black Forays”. Subjects possess an 8% higher mass of the lungs, heart, stomach and brain as well as a number of altercations on the physiological level. The bloodstream carries an unusually high white blood cell count and an unidentifiable hormone that allows natural regeneration to occur a recorded 12x faster than the average human. Subjects experience abnormally elongated bursts of adrenaline due to an increase in testosterone and the presence of an unidentifiable hormone replacing cortisol. Altered temperamental attributes include a shorter temper, fatigue, soreness and a previously unheard of craving for protein-rich foods.&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-119076-2&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Subjects do not use oxygen in natural bodily processes, instead anomalously utilizing the element argon to function. The subjects are able to survive on the low percentages of argon present in Earth’s atmosphere but are unable to exercise and perform strenuous labor without suffering from an argon variant of hypoxia. However, when utilizing a breathing tank composed of pure argon, subjects show steadily-increasing, improved capabilities including a range of stamina, speed and strength 12x higher than the average human.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discovery&lt;/strong&gt;: On 12/29/██, SCP-5587 was discovered after a string of disappearances occurred near Mount Eisenhower. A group of hikers vanished on the mountain and the search party disappeared soon after. A foundation agent stationed at the ████ Lodge in ███████ Notch followed the authorities’ trail and discovered SCP-5587, briefly entering SCP-5587-A. Shortly after exiting, he was found dead by a passerby on the main trail. Notified of his death, the foundation closed off nearby hiking trails and Mobile Task Force Zeta-12 was sent to investigate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;+&amp;nbsp;Recovered&amp;nbsp;Footage&amp;nbsp;of&amp;nbsp;Zeta-12&#039;s&amp;nbsp;Exploration&amp;nbsp;of&amp;nbsp;SCP-5587-A&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Close&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;blockquote&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Foreword:&lt;/strong&gt; The following footage of Zeta-12’s exploration of SCP-5587-A was recovered from the helmet camera of Zeta-12’s Captain White.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;lt;Begin Log 1500 hours&amp;gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Mobile Task Force Zeta-12 successfully enters SCP-5587-A. Video feed shows all six members fanning out around the immediate area, rifles at the ready.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Command:&lt;/strong&gt; Captain, do you copy?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Yes Ma’am. Do you have visuals?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Footage pans upwards revealing SCP-5587-A’s turquoise trees and saturated flora peppering the landscape. Fuzzy patches of turquoise swaths linger about the tree trunks.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Command:&lt;/strong&gt; Affirmative. Look around, is the gateway accessible on your side?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Yes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Command:&lt;/strong&gt; Then proceed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Alright! Let’s go boys, keep formation and move out.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bridger:&lt;/strong&gt; Which direction Cap&#039;n? There’s no path.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;White checks the compass swinging from her belt.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; We’ll move east.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Camera pans eastward, revealing a swath of bright orange fungi blocking the way forwards.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Nevermind. We’re going west instead. Polonskye, take the lead. Nickelson, take the back and mark where we&#039;ve been. Let&#039;s move.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Zeta-12 moves westward through the trees for approximately six minutes.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bridger:&lt;/strong&gt; Hey Cap’n&amp;#8230;does this place seem&amp;#8230;quiet to you? It&#039;s just fungus out here and nothin’ else.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; There&#039;s no wind or heat signatures on infrared besides us. That&#039;s why.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alejo:&lt;/strong&gt; No heat signatures &lt;em&gt;yet.&lt;/em&gt; This place could be quiet because all the critters are staying clear of something bigger.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;A short burst of disgruntled chatter ensues and Zeta-12 continues their path through SCP-5587-A.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Command:&lt;/strong&gt; Captain, stop.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;White pauses and signals at the others.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Ma&#039;am?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Command:&lt;/strong&gt; Please collect samples from the local flora.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Yes ma’am. Alejo, Jamie, you’re carrying the sample kits. Command wants samples from both the fungi and trees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Jamie cautiously approaches a turquoise tree with Alejo in suit.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jamie:&lt;/strong&gt; Think this thing will come alive and eat one of us?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alejo:&lt;/strong&gt; Likely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jamie:&lt;/strong&gt; I’m loving your positive attitude.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Footage shows Zeta-12 standing at attention around Alejo and Jamie. Jamie holds out a container and a silver blade. She slices off a sliver of the tree’s unnaturally smooth bark then caps the container and places the sample in her pack. Alejo mimics the action with a nearby group of colorful fungi. Both stand and return to their positions within the group.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Ready to go?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Jamie flashes a thumbs up.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Then let’s keep moving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Zeta-12 continues moving west for about twenty yards.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Command:&lt;/strong&gt; Captain, are any of you experiencing shortness of breath or fatigue?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; No ma’am, not that I’m aware of. Why?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jamie:&lt;/strong&gt; What’s command saying?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Command:&lt;/strong&gt; Atmosphere composition readings from your helmets have just been received on our end. The atmosphere is primarily composed of argon gas. No oxygen has been detected. Hypothetically, you should have suffocated the moment you entered SCP-5587-A.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;White repeats the message from command out loud.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jamie:&lt;/strong&gt; That’s quite reassuring. Good to know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Command, there are no issues on our end. Should we continue?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Command:&lt;/strong&gt; Yes. Continue your mission and immediately notify us if any changes arise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Yes ma’am.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Zeta-12 continues a westward path through the trees in silence. Twelve yards later the team is stopped by Polonskye positioned in front. He motions for White and the camera is brought forward, pointing down at a messy heap of human bones and viscera splattered piled on the ground. A quick observation of the surrounding area reveals large claw marks and torn scraps of cloth strewn across nearby flora.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jamie:&lt;/strong&gt; Hey Alejo, remember when you said something about ‘something bigger’ earlier?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Command, it looks like we&#039;ve found the remains of those missing hikers and police from the initial report. Orders?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Command:&lt;/strong&gt; Continue your path and keep an eye out for the entity responsible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Yes ma&#039;am.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Footage pans around to the rest of Zeta-12.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Listen, I want all of you on high alert from now on forwards. Don’t break formation and keep your rifles ready. We don’t know anything about what we’re dealing with, only that it’s hostile.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alejo:&lt;/strong&gt; Look at the size of those claw marks. I think I can safely say it’s huge and it&#039;s dangerous.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Command:&lt;/strong&gt; Captain, move on and continue your mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Yes ma’am.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;White motions for the others to continue onward. The team moves approximately six yards through the trees until a faint, low growling is picked up by audio feed.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jamie:&lt;/strong&gt; Anyone else hear that?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Zeta-12 stops and White gives the order to move into defensive positioning. The low growling gradually increases in volume, coming from further ahead.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; We’ll keep moving forwards. Slowly. Stay sharp, keep your weapons at the ready.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At the front, Nickelson raises her magnification goggles.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nickelson:&lt;/strong&gt; Wait–I have eyes on something. Big heat signature. Four hundred yards down that way through the trees. Huge fuckin’ bear thing. Headed right up this way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; How big?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nickleson:&lt;/strong&gt; Gotta be at least ten feet high.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Alright. Ready up boys, we’re holding our ground. Nickelson, what else can you tell us?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nickelson:&lt;/strong&gt; It&#039;s blue and its got &lt;em&gt;enormous&lt;/em&gt; fucking claws–that’s gotta be what tore up those people back there. It’s running through the trees right for us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; How fast is it moving? Would it be possible to outrun?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nickelson:&lt;/strong&gt; Hell no-It’s already two hundred yards closer. It&#039;s got this big lumbering gait. You can see it clearly now, it’s closing in fast enough.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; You got that, command?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Command:&lt;/strong&gt; Affirmative. Continue holding your ground. You have permission to engage the entity and apply lethal force as needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Nickelson lowers her goggles as the growling continues to increase. She falls in line with the rest of Zeta-12’s defensive position, firearm at the ready.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Footage pans over through the trees where SCP-5587-B is seen charging through the woods making a beeline for Zeta-12. Entity is fifty yards away and closing in.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Hold steady. Fire on my command.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The rumbling grows louder as the ursine entity lumbers through the trees, bearing down on Zeta-12 at thirty yards.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Hold…hold…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5587-B charges into the immediate area, letting out a roar and revealing an array of massive canines.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jamie:&lt;/strong&gt; Holy shit!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Fire!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Bullets fired at SCP-5587-B ineffectively bounce off its fur and the entity does not slow its charge, instead lurching onto its hind legs and towering over the formation of Zeta-12.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;White:&lt;/strong&gt; Fall back! Scatter and fall back!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Footage is scrambled as White dives backwards, narrowly missing a swipe of SCP-5587-B’s paw. Video feed is rightened as White stands and fires more rounds into the SCP-5587-B. The entity roars before bearing down on White.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;White attempts to dive out of the way but the entity’s claws snare her arm, knocking her rifle from her grip and throwing her to the ground. White struggles to draw her emergency blade. Incoherent shouting and more gunfire from the other Zeta-12 members can be heard in the background. The footage abruptly ends as SCP-5587-B swipes at White’s head with its other paw, ripping through her helmet and damaging the camera.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;lt;End Log 1537 hours&amp;gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Closing Statement:&lt;/strong&gt; All six members of Zeta-12 exited SCP-5587 alive despite bearing extensive injuries. Recorded injuries included numerous lacerations, bruises, one case of head trauma and three cases of broken bones. Immediately after exiting SCP-5587, the entire Task Force collapsed due to heavy blood loss and were immediately lifted to Site-17 for medical treatment and psychological evaluation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;+&amp;nbsp;SCP-5587-6&#039;s&amp;nbsp;Psychological&amp;nbsp;Evaluation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Close&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Below is a transcript of Captain White’s psychological evaluation conducted shortly after she regained consciousness in Site-17’s hospital wing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;blockquote&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interviewed:&lt;/strong&gt; Mobile Task Force Zeta-12 Black Foray Captain White, now designated SCP-5587-6.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interviewer:&lt;/strong&gt; Researcher Lawson&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Foreword:&lt;/strong&gt; Interview was conducted at SCP-5587-6&#039;s hospital bedside. She is in treatment for lacerations, head trauma and a fractured wrist.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;lt;Begin Log, 1200 Hours&amp;gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Researcher Lawson:&lt;/strong&gt; How are you feeling?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5587-6:&lt;/strong&gt; Where am I? Where’s the rest of my team?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Researcher Lawson:&lt;/strong&gt; You and the rest of Zeta-12 are at an undisclosed foundation site.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5587-6:&lt;/strong&gt; Are they alive?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Researcher Lawson:&lt;/strong&gt; Yes, your team members are in stable recovery. Now, how are &lt;em&gt;you&lt;/em&gt; feeling?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5587-6:&lt;/strong&gt; Uh..gh&amp;#8230;Mentally or physically?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Researcher Lawson:&lt;/strong&gt; Both.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5587-6:&lt;/strong&gt; Sore. Mostly just tired. Glad everyone made it out, though. Can I see them?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Researcher Lawson:&lt;/strong&gt; Not yet. All six of you are still in recovery. Now, I’ve got some questions for you about your experience in SCP-5587-A. Firstly, can you recall the events that happened while you were in SCP-5587-A?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5587-6 gingerly massages her temple.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5587-6:&lt;/strong&gt; Sorry, the head’s still wicked sore. Details are a little uh&amp;#8230;what’s the word&amp;#8230;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SCP-5587-6 pauses for a few seconds&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5587-6:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;#8230;uh &lt;em&gt;disoriented&lt;/em&gt; yeah, disoriented&amp;#8230;right now. Our whole mission was taped though so everything that happened should be there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Researcher Lawson:&lt;/strong&gt; Our analysts were only able to salvage the recording up until SCP-5587-B knocked you down and damaged your helmet camera. There’s no record about what events that happened after you were knocked down. Can you recall anything?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5587-6:&lt;/strong&gt; 5587-B? Is that what you’re calling that thing that came after us?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Researcher Lawson nods.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5587-6:&lt;/strong&gt; Well&amp;#8230;I can remember&amp;#8230;flashes. Everything got blurry after that bear put a paw through my helmet. I stabbed it at one point&amp;#8230;the thing definitely bled although it was this&amp;#8230;blue color. Bridger and Jamie were yelling and I think they drew it off me. Then&amp;#8230;it was just&amp;#8230;lumbering about everywhere, attacking everyone. Bullets weren’t doing anything to it. I remember giving the order to fall back to the rift and then we ran…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Researcher Lawson:&lt;/strong&gt; All the way back? Even with your wounds?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5587-6:&lt;/strong&gt; I&amp;#8230;I guess so. I remember running and then seeing the rift in front of me again. I don’t know how we made it. Maybe it was just one hell of a reaction to the pain?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Researcher Lawson:&lt;/strong&gt; That’s one possibility. Now, is there anything else you can remember? Any specific details?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5587-6:&lt;/strong&gt; No&amp;#8230;I think I’m still&amp;#8230;processing everything. All I know is that we went in, got attacked by the bear and almost didn’t make it back out. If I can remember anything else, I’ll let you know as soon as possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Researcher Lawson:&lt;/strong&gt; Thank you. Now, you’re expected to be cleared by the doctor this afternoon although you and the rest of Zeta-12 will remain in the hospital for more tests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5587-6:&lt;/strong&gt; Is there something wrong with us?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Researcher Lawson:&lt;/strong&gt; That’s unclear at the moment but rest assured, there’s no need to worry. Medical staff say that none of you are at risk of dying.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5587-6:&lt;/strong&gt; Well, at least we’re alive. Thank you, doctor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Researcher Lawson:&lt;/strong&gt; You’re welcome. Now I believe that concludes our time together. I appreciate your cooperation, I’ll leave you to rest now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;lt;End Log, 1220 hours&amp;gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Closing Statement:&lt;/strong&gt; Approximately 6 hours after psychological evaluations concluded, all six members of Zeta-12 successfully cleared medical examination.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Addendum 5587.1:&lt;/strong&gt; On 1/4/██ SCP-5587-1 through -6 were transferred to a permanent, shared containment cell due to the identical nature of their anomalous properties. In the following days after initial transfer, subjects began experiencing worsening symptoms of fatigue.&lt;br /&gt;
On 1/10/██ at 1325 hours, SCP-5587-1 was observed through camera feed to be attempting a full set of pushups. Three minutes in, all six subjects suddenly collapsed unconscious onto the floor of their containment and were immediately transported to the hospital wing. Blood tests revealed the subjects’ utilization of argon and all six were promptly administered argon breathing tubes. Subjects made a full recovery within twenty-four hours.&lt;br /&gt;
SCP-5587-1 through -6&#039;s joint containment cell has since been fitted with a regulated gas pipe pumping argon into the atmosphere per the subjects’ needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Addendum 5587.2:&lt;/strong&gt; After █ years of containment, conditioning and specialized training overseen by Researcher Lawson, SCP-5587-1 through -6 have repeatedly requested to return to the Mobile Task Force mission field. Due to their enhanced physical abilities under the influence of argon, the subjects have been speculated to pose as a tactical advantage in the mission field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As of &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: line-through;&quot;&gt;3/14/██&lt;/span&gt; 6/14/██, the O5 Council&#039;s permission for SCP-5587-1 through -6 to return to the Mobile Task Force mission field &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: line-through;&quot;&gt;is pending&lt;/span&gt; has been granted given specific requirements in regards to assigned missions&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-119076-3&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; are met.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As of 7/4/██, subjects have been re-designated as MTF Zeta-12 &amp;quot;Argon Breathers&amp;quot;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnotes-footer&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Footnotes&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-119076-1&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;. Protons and electrons are impossibly distorted.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-119076-2&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;2&lt;/a&gt;. Subjects’ bodies demand more proteins for the growth of new molecular pathways.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-119076-3&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;3&lt;/a&gt;. Missions must be short and call for deadly force.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footer-wikiwalk-nav&quot;&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#171; &lt;a class=&quot;newpage&quot; href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5586&quot;&gt;SCP-5586&lt;/a&gt; | SCP-5587 | &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5588&quot;&gt;SCP-5588&lt;/a&gt; &amp;#187;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/solius&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5319086&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1607830220&quot; alt=&quot;solius&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5319086)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/solius&quot;  &gt;solius&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
